Fix for dev-cpp/glibmm-2.66.8 (giomm-2.4, SLOT 2) building against
newer glib (>=2.89.2, e.g. dev-libs/glib-2.89.4), matching the fix
already carried by dev-cpp/glibmm-2.88.1-r666::Miezhiko (SLOT 2.68)
for the same issue -- see that overlay's
glibmm-2.88.1-gdbusactiongroup-emblem-final-types.patch and
glibmm-2.88.1-dbusactiongroup-final-type-check.patch, backports of
upstream glibmm commits 00508a702de117967ee8ae8c70f3786c4d73f958 and
289433385cb9d94e87e18a226042a0334cf1c947.

Newer glib declares GDBusActionGroup and GEmblem via
G_DECLARE_FINAL_TYPE, which auto-generates a typedef for
GDBusActionGroupClass/GEmblemClass. glibmm-2.66.8's *pre-generated*
giomm-2.4 headers, shipped under untracked/gio/giomm/ in the release
tarball (meson builds directly from these -- gmmproc/mm-common is not
re-run, so patching the gio/src/*.hg m4 sources has no effect on the
actual build), unconditionally declare their own `using X = struct _X`
alias for the same names, causing:

  untracked/gio/giomm/dbusactiongroup.h:32:7: error: conflicting
  declaration 'using GDBusActionGroupClass =
  struct _GDBusActionGroupClass'
  note: previous declaration as 'typedef struct GDBusActionGroupClass
  GDBusActionGroupClass' (from glib's G_DECLARE_FINAL_TYPE)

  untracked/gio/giomm/emblem.h:31:7: error: conflicting declaration
  'using GEmblemClass = struct _GEmblemClass'

This patches the shipped generated headers directly (not the .hg
sources) and guards the alias behind a glib version check, so both
succeed compiling against glib >= 2.89.2. It does not backport the
upstream _DO_NOT_DERIVE_GTYPE/_ABI_AS_WITH_DERIVED_GTYPE/
_STRUCT_NOT_HIDDEN changes to the generated derived-GType boilerplate
(that would require re-running gmmproc); this is enough to fix the
build for consumers, such as media-gfx/inkscape, that don't derive
custom GTypes from Gio::DBus::ActionGroup or Gio::Emblem.

--- a/untracked/gio/giomm/dbusactiongroup.h
+++ b/untracked/gio/giomm/dbusactiongroup.h
@@ -29,7 +29,15 @@

 #ifndef DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS
 using GDBusActionGroup = struct _GDBusActionGroup;
+// GDBusActionGroup was declared a final type between GLib 2.89.1 and 2.89.2.
+// Before that, GDBusActionGroupClass was not declared in GLib.
+// The preprocessor macro G_DBUS_ACTION_GROUP_CLASS was defined, though.
+#if !GLIB_CHECK_VERSION(2,89,1) || (!GLIB_CHECK_VERSION(2,89,2) && defined(G_DBUS_ACTION_GROUP_CLASS))
+  // glib < 2.89.1 or (glib == 2.89.1 and G_DBUS_ACTION_GROUP_CLASS is a preprocessor macro)
+  // GDBusActionGroup is not a final type,
+  // GDBusActionGroupClass is not declared in GLib.
 using GDBusActionGroupClass = struct _GDBusActionGroupClass;
+#endif
 #endif /* DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS */


--- a/untracked/gio/giomm/emblem.h
+++ b/untracked/gio/giomm/emblem.h
@@ -24,11 +24,16 @@

 #include <glibmm/object.h>
 #include <giomm/icon.h>
+#include <gio/gio.h>


 #ifndef DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS
 using GEmblem = struct _GEmblem;
+// Newer glib (>= 2.89.2) declares GEmblem as G_DECLARE_FINAL_TYPE, which
+// already provides a typedef for GEmblemClass.
+#if !GLIB_CHECK_VERSION(2,89,2)
 using GEmblemClass = struct _GEmblemClass;
+#endif
 #endif /* DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS */
